035111652442369,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the day of the week on which Kim's birthday fell, we need to calculate the day of the week 200 days ago from today, which is Wednesday. We can do this by finding the remainder when 200 is divided by 7, since there are 7 days in a week.\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\n\\[ 200 \\div 7 = 28 \\text{ R } 4 \\]\n\nThis means that 200 days is equivalent to 28 weeks and 4 extra days. Since 28 weeks is a whole number of weeks, it brings us back to the same day of the week. Therefore, we only need to count back 4 days from Wednesday.\n\nCounting back 4 days from Wednesday:\n\n1. One day before Wednesday is Tuesday.\n2. Two days before Wednesday is Monday.\n3. Three days before Wednesday is Sunday.\n4. Four days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nTherefore, Kim's birthday fell on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To determine the day of the week on which Kim's birthday fell, we need to calculate the day of the week 200 days ago from today, which is Wednesday. We can do this by finding the remainder when 200 is divided by 7, since there are 7 days in a week.\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\n\\[ 200 \\div 7 = 28 \\text{ R } 4 \\]\n\nThis means that 200 days is equivalent to 28 weeks and 4 extra days. Since 28 weeks is a whole number of weeks, it brings us back to the same day of the week. Therefore, we only need to count back 4 days from Wednesday.\n\nCounting back 4 days from Wednesday:\n\n1. One day before Wednesday is Tuesday.\n2. Two days before Wednesday is Monday.\n3. Three days before Wednesday is Sunday.\n4. Four days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nTherefore, Kim's birthday fell on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\).","id":"number_theory:49"}
